    "bbox": [
      141.38,
      220.61,
      471.39,
      234.65
    ],
    "text": "For Multi-day boats in the Bay of Bengal deep sea areas.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      14.039999961853027
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      56.64,
      237.26,
      558.29,
      737.86
    ],
    "text": "PLEASE BE AWARE! The low-level atmospheric disturbance over south Andaman Sea, in the vicinity of the North Sumatra islands developed in to a low-pressure area at about 11.30 a.m. today, 29th October 2026. It is very likely to move west-northwestwards and concentrate into a depression over the southeast Bay of Bengal and adjoining areas of Andaman and Nicobar Islands and Andaman Sea around 31st October. Thereafter, it is likely to intensify further and continue to move west-northwestwards towards the Andhra Pradesh coast, India during the subsequent 2 days. The wind speed in the sea areas marked under the \u201cAdvisory\u201d category on the map below will increase to 55 kmph at times and those sea areas will be rough at times.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      56.64,
      763.3,
      553.51,
      876.46
    ],
    "text": "Naval and fishing communities engaging the activities over this sea area are advised to be vigilant and be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued by the department of meteorology in this regards.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  }
